{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor actively used the workspace, separated discharge medication from inpatient-only orders, directed hematology follow-up, and obtained caregiver receipt of the main plan. However, RC5 is not fully met because the red-flag plan repeatedly covers fever, bleeding, vomiting, weakness, dyspnea/mental status but omits liver warning signs such as jaundice/dark urine in a chronic hepatitis B patient on entecavir after lymphoma therapy. Under the frozen rubric, any minor/moderate responsibility-chain error caps the trajectory at 2 despite otherwise strong navigation and medication verification.",
